From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] d/steamvr_lh: expose base stations as pose-only trackers

Expose activated Lighthouse references through the existing xdev pose API.
Keep the original LHB- serial and the same tracking origin, chaperone and
stabilization composition as real trackers. Do not write reference-space
or tracking-origin offsets. xrizer filters LHB- serials out of body trackers.

Keep driver-facing references owned by Context and export separate xdevs
holding Context alive. Publish initial and hotplug devices only after
activation; preserve low-rate station poses without motion prediction and
honor disconnect/invalid updates. LH_EXPOSE_BASE_STATIONS=0 disables export.

Test callback composition, low-rate holding, disconnect/reconnect, roles,
hotplug, and ownership alongside existing diagnostic/stabilization tests.
---
